# THE BRANCH IS THE BUILD, AND THAT INCLUDES THE FILES THAT DESCRIBE IT. Pages serves cf-live
# verbatim, so anything committed here is downloadable -- which is why check_site.py lives on
# master and says so at the top of itself. Two files were missed by that reasoning, and both
# answered 200 on 28 Aug 2026:
#
#     /CLAUDE.md                          12,324 b   branch layout, the deploy gate, the fact that
#                                                    administrators can bypass a red check, and
#                                                    since today the purge procedure and the
#                                                    obfuscation switch
#     /.github/workflows/site-checks.yml   2,933 b   what the required check does, the sha it is
#                                                    pinned to, and by omission what it does NOT
#                                                    verify
#
# The second is the more useful of the two to anybody probing the site: it names the gate and its
# blind spots. Neither is a secret -- there are no credentials in either -- but neither is a page,
# and a static host with no build step cannot tell the difference without being told.
#
# NEITHER FILE CAN SIMPLY MOVE. CLAUDE.md is the guide for whoever is working ON this branch, so
# hosting it elsewhere defeats it; the workflow must live here because it triggers on pushes to
# here. So they stay committed and stop being served.
#
# LAST IN THE FILE, DELIBERATELY, and this is a budget decision rather than tidiness. Pages honours
# the first 100 rules; /dist/* above is #97 and the note beside it depends on that. Inserting these
# ABOVE it would push it to #99 and quietly spend two thirds of the remaining margin. Appended
# here, /dist/* keeps its slot, these are #98 and #99, and nothing that already works moves. Safe
# because first-match-wins and /dist/* only matches paths under /dist/.
#
# 301 rather than 404 because a 404 status in this file is IGNORED -- measured, see the note on the
# error page above. A redirect is what Pages actually honours, so a redirect is what this is.
/CLAUDE.md / 301
/.github/* / 301
